        <h2>Entry 12</h2>  
        <p>I arrived at the far north side of the mostly unexplored continet in the early morning. Walking off the steam boat I was taken a back by the stench. It smelt sick. I walked along the coast at first taking in the sights.</p>
        <p>There were waves of sand being blown by the misty wind obscuring my vision.</p>
        <p>I decided it was time to move inland.</p>
        <p>I never saw anything alive. Just dunes, the wind, and every so often a small flicker in the corner of my eye. It's starting to scare me.</p>
        <p>"We are a long way from home." the professor said as he finished reading the long dead mans diary.</p>

